      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "@id": "https://www.stselectronicrecyclinginc.com/bakersfield-ca#faqpage",
      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What areas do you serve for electronics recycling in Bakersfield?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "We provide complimentary pickup throughout Bakersfield, Kern County and the greater San Joaquin Valley including energy sites, agricultural facilities, healthcare campuses and school districts. Service is scheduled to minimize operational disruption for enterprise clients near Highway 99 and Highway 58."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What certifications and standards do you follow?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "We maintain NIST 800-88 Rev. 2 compliant destruction, support HIPAA technical safeguards under 45 CFR §164.312, ISO 27001 aligned processes and RIOS standards. All work includes serialized chain of custody documentation and accurate reporting suitable for audits. Equipment collected in Bakersfield is transported to our certified processing facilities in Jacksonville, Texas and Houston, Texas."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is pickup really free in Bakersfield?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Pickup is complimentary for qualifying volumes. We provide transparent pricing with no hidden fees and asset recovery credits where applicable to help offset costs for Bakersfield organizations. Most compliance officers at organizations like California Resources Corporation and Kern High School District expect this model."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can you handle large scale ITAD projects in Kern County?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. Our 200,000 sq ft operation regularly manages enterprise ITAD, data center decommissioning and multi-site healthcare or government equipment refreshes with coordinated scheduling and complete documentation. STS engagements with large employers typically include weekend or off-hours coordination to avoid business interruption."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do you provide certificates of destruction?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. Every engagement includes serial-number specific certificates of destruction detailing method, weight, and downstream facility. This documentation supports HIPAA, SOX, GLBA and other regulatory audits for Bakersfield healthcare, financial and government clients."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How do you protect data during electronics recycling?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "We use NIST 800-88 Rev. 2 compliant data sanitization methods including physical destruction and cryptographic erasure. All processes maintain chain of custody documentation from Bakersfield pickup through final processing at our certified facilities in Jacksonville and Houston, Texas."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do you offer on-site data destruction in Bakersfield?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. On-site hard drive shredding and witnessed destruction services are available for Bakersfield organizations requiring immediate data sanitization at their facility. This is standard for government agencies, financial institutions and healthcare providers with strict security requirements."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What industries do you serve in Kern County?",
